<%# The span's grade affordance on the event row — a "grade" button that opens the
    span-grading drawer (into the shared turbo-frame, like a drilled-down action), plus
    the span's current Alex grade + McRitchie audit markers. Markers are server-rendered
    from the passed grades (so the integration/component tests and a no-JS load see
    them), and bound to the row's Alpine `grades` state so a drawer save updates them
    live via the hb:span-graded CustomEvent. @click.stop keeps the grade button from
    toggling the span's expand/collapse. Locals: event, alex (ActionGrade | nil),
    mcr (ActionGrade | nil). %>
<td class="hb-evtfbcell" data-test="event-grade-cell" @click.stop>
  <button type="button" class="hb-btn hb-gradebtn" data-test="event-grade-open"
          @click="openDrawer('<%= heartbeat_event_feedback_path(event) %>')">grade &#9656;</button>
  <span class="hb-evtmarks">
    <%= render "heartbeat/event_grade_mark", grader: "alex", grade: alex %>
    <%= render "heartbeat/event_grade_mark", grader: "mcr", grade: mcr %>
  </span>
</td>
